wensu (formerly scholar-search)
===============================

Version: 0.4.0 (2026-10-23)

Academic search: a read-only, microkernel-based scholarly metadata service.

This project is an independent, non-official tool. It is not affiliated with,
endorsed by, or sponsored by any academic database operator.


Provenance and third-party notices
----------------------------------

This codebase was written for this project. No source files, modules or functions
were copied from another repository. What it does reuse is narrower than "code":

  1. CSS selector strings that identify elements on CNKI pages. These are facts
     about a public web page (class names, ids), not creative expression; they
     were checked against live pages and are covered by fixture tests.
  2. The order of the interaction steps (open search page, fill box, submit,
     read grid), which is dictated by how the site works.
  3. Knowledge of known pitfalls, such as the hidden captcha widget that stays in
     the DOM, which would otherwise produce false positives.

Those were informed by three public MIT-licensed projects:

  cookjohn/cnki-skills        https://github.com/cookjohn/cnki-skills
  SepineTam/cnki-mcp          https://github.com/SepineTam/cnki-mcp
  wuruiqi/cnki-mcp            https://github.com/wuruiqi/cnki-mcp

All three are MIT-licensed. This project is MIT-licensed as well, so the terms are
compatible either way; the attribution above is given because it is the right
thing to do, not because a licence compels it for the three items listed.

What was NOT taken from them: the browser transport (they drive a debug port; this
project uses a browser extension plus a native messaging host), the microkernel
and channel layout, the policy/quota/risk engine, the parsers, the export layer,
and every line of Python, JavaScript, C# and PowerShell in this repository.

If you believe a fragment here is derived from your work in a way this notice does
not describe, open an issue and it will be corrected or removed.

See docs/reference-parity.md for a feature-by-feature comparison, including where
this project deliberately diverges.


